// ADR-0002: no `replace` directive is ever checked in. This workspace is what
// gives local development the sibling-on-disk resolution instead, and flipping
// GOWORK=off exercises the resolution a real consumer gets.
//
// ADR-0001 sets the floor at go 1.27, not yet GA. Until it is, the floor is
// go 1.26, tracked by #366 and reverted the day 1.27 ships. errors.AsType is
// what holds it at 1.26. No file in this repository carries a `toolchain`
// directive; a consumer resolves the floor with whatever toolchain they have.
go 1.26

use (
	.
	./driver/env
	./driver/http
	./driver/kv
	./driver/windows
	./driver/yaml
	./examples
)
